From 2a526f52d81944a8f78e1f581b321b86bfa2bfcd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:04:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] python: a strategy interpreter and the draws a Hypothesis
 frontend needs

hegel._native gains TestCase.generate, which walks a CompiledStrategy (a
frontend's strategy compiled into a tree of primitive draws, collections
under the frontend's own continuation protocol, choices between
alternatives, mapped, built and filtered values, and opaque leaves the
frontend draws itself) against the live test case in one call, recording
the choices it makes for the frontend's bookkeeping. With it the five
small entry points a frontend built on another API needs: a weighted
integer draw carrying shrink_towards, a forced integer draw, a text
generator over explicit codepoint ranges, a live case's choices as a
blob, and a test case replaying a blob outside a run. Nothing changes for
hegel.generators. Ported from the Hypothesis-side extension of the
experiment running Hypothesis on libhegel, and Hypothesis-agnostic: the
frontend passes its draw, record and invalid callbacks and its retry
exception.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016mTrLpQ8SJg9RC9F1GH9Ac
